        "reviews": "“No section feels frustrating, but rather challenging. Every mistake and every death is a product of our skill, not the game's mechanics. This fosters a constant desire for &quot;one more try&quot; and transforms Go Slimey Go! into the memorable pixel art platformer we hoped it would be.”<br>10 – PressOver<br><br>“Go Slimey Go! is my favorite 2D platformer of 2025 [...] You may not have the same emotional resonance as Celeste, but [this game] made me feel the same platforming bliss.”<br>Second Wind<br><br>“The title stands as a prime example of what indie talent can offer without the massive budgets of big franchises. Go Slimey Go! doesn't rely on massive marketing or big promises, but rather on a simple yet effective design and gameplay that hooks you from the very first moment.”<br>Kotaku<br>",
